{"body":{"text":["The chassis does for every component what each would else do for itself, reads being, in the author's words, the \"state management\" of the \"framework\" (21/31). It asks the reads of one turn of every component as one read of the engine, kept live, each told its own part of the answer, and each asked alone again where that one read fails; renders a component again when what it is given changes, or an answer says something new, and lays the new render over the page, changing only what differs, so focus, a caret and a scroll stay (21/59, 21/61); keeps each drawing in place by its key, a holon by its id, a drawing by the uses it was reached through; shows a drawing made anew, or a render waiting on its reads, once every read within it has answered, so nothing shows piece by piece, or after two seconds; and stands each drawing as a boundary, the component Problem drawn in its place, given what failed, where what it is given, a read it asks or its render fails (21/39). Where the way back finds no change, the chassis marks the place fixed, a fact of the place no render undoes. It draws nothing a person sees beyond a host for each drawing: the inspector and the bar showing the page busy are the page's (21/33). A component holding what the browser keeps for it, as the input does with what is typed and what completion offers, gives its node with how to update it, and is updated in place of rendering. *The chassis's work the session's, at the author's word (21/25, 21/31, 21/35, 21/71); built, 271 tests passing.*"]},"id":"1M86HMN933NN000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}